# Base URL of the Jahez API, INCLUDING the version prefix and without a trailing slash.
# It is read at BUILD time (Vite inlines VITE_* variables), so set it in the environment of
# the build that produces the bundle you deploy. There is deliberately no fallback value.
#
# Development (jahez_api served by `php artisan serve`):
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
#
# Production (Docker image): the same-origin path. nginx forwards /api/ to the API
# container (docker/nginx.conf), so the browser never calls another origin:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
# A separate public API origin also works (never localhost), for example
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.org/api/v1
#
# Whenever the API is on another origin (development, or the absolute form above), the
# API must list this app's exact origin in its CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS
# (development: http://localhost:3000 - the port is pinned in vite.config.ts).
